WEBVTT

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:12.360
"Kodomo no Omocha"

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.890
and your bitter face and bitter
feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.350
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.900
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.910
I may be a little jumbled,
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.920
Keep your eyes on me, okay!?

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:37.780
I'm so glad... I met you...

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:43.040
D- Dad?

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.460
You can't die yet!

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.790
No!

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:52.130
No!!

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:57.130
"Spring Comes In an Avalanche of Tears"

00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:03.470
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh? What's going on?
Where's the usual "I'm Kurata Sana" part?

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:07.520
Don't tell me we're going to
plunge on into the serious stuff!

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.150
E- everyone,

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:13.780
the graduation ceremony is nearly here.

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:18.070
"Graduation project"

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.280
So I'd like to have everyone
make something to leave behind

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.070
to commemorate your graduation.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:23.080
And so... and so... I think our class
should c- c- create a monument this big...

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:27.500
you see...

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.500
Please! Everyone, listen!

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.090
Wipe up that nosebleed.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.420
Y- you're all listening to me?

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:37.420
Sensei was thinking that
we could all create a monument

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.090
--made from the shapes of our faces.
--Sana-chan stayed home again today, huh?

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.760
--I mean, am I right? Sure I am.
--Mm-hmm. It must have been
a shock for her, all right.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.560
--Nothing else would leave a
greater reminder of who you are.
--Akito-kun, aren't you concerned?

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.060
--Nothing else would leave a
greater reminder of who you are.
--What could have happened to Sana-chan,

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.430
--Nothing else would leave a
greater reminder of who you are.
--anyway, anyway, anyway-

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.440
Thank you for dinner.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:56.110
Sana-chan, you should
really eat at least a little bit.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.740
I'm sorry, Shimura-san.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:02.700
I know you made it for me, but my appetite
seems to have gotten lost.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:04.450
Mama,

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.790
I'm sorry, but may I be
excused to my room?

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.460
Yes, you may.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.120
I'm sorry.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.790
If you're leaving that, can I have it?

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:16.460
Let's release a CD, Sana-chan! A CD!

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.470
Sensei, you didn't have to do that.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:23.140
I just want to give Sana some time alone.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:27.270
Yes, you're right. It has been a week
since Gojo-san passed away.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.810
She has recently started talking
to us a little, at least.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.730
But she can't go on like this forever.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.730
Haven't you noticed?

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:42.160
Not once since Gojo-san died
has she shed a single tear.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:52.120
She... doesn't know how she
should be taking Gojo-san's death.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:03.130
If she would shed some tears,
it would alleviate her sorrow somewhat.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:08.140
But she does not know how to cry.
No- she isn't trying to cry.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:10.480
Oh... then, what should we do?

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.310
Right now, all we can do
is silently watch over her.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.360
You lied to me...

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.780
I'll always be by your side.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.160
You lied to me...

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.160
I lied, all right!

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:29.660
There's no way I would die!

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.830
We fooled you!

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:32.750
We fooled the idol!

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.080
Smile, we tricked you!

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.080
--You're on "Fool The Candid Idol"

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:36.960
"Airing Dogdays at 6:00!!"

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.750
Wow, that was a convincing fake death!

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.340
Should I die even more
ostentatiously next time?

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.760
You tricked me!!

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:48.430
That was mean, Take-chan!
I thought you were really dead!

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:49.760
S- sorry about that.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.270
Relax. I'll always be at your side.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:01.900
You lied to me.
You're not at my side, are you?

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:06.030
You lied to me...

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.380
Kurata?

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.060
That barbecue was fun, huh?

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:42.070
There on that veranda,
with a nighttime view.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:46.280
It really was fun, Take-chan.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:57.750
Dumbass!

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.750
Hayama...

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:04.760
What are you doing?
You almost got run over, you know!

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:09.760
I was wondering if Take-chan's...
if Take-chan's ghost will appear.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:12.760
Ghost?

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:15.100
Ah, it's snowing.

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:16.520
Come to think of it,

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:20.900
I had that snowball fight with Take-chan
at Yatsugatake. That was fun.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:26.440
I wish I could see you, Take-chan.
Even your ghost would be okay.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:30.110
I know. If I die too, I can see Take-chan-

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:31.990
What are you doing, Hayama?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.870
Take-chan...

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:40.500
I can't make any cracks today!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.420
Where did you go this morning?

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:45.090
Nowhere. For a walk.

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:49.760
We've got a planning meeting for a
new drama today. You have to cheer up.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.760
Click!

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.390
--♪ Gotta be in wide-open top form,
whirring around on Komawari power. ♪

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.180
--You've cheered up?

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.430
--Babbit can dance too, right?

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:59.100
♪ In top form today,
and top form tomorrow, too! ♪

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:02.440
♪ Don't give in, fight on,
poppy-pop-pop-pop! ♪

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.110
Like that.

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.110
Come on, let's dance together!

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.780
Don't dance in the car!

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.780
Ah! I made a wisecrack! Yahoo!

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:13.120
I'm sorry. I don't feel like it today.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.120
Sana-chan...

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.450
Front teeth go boom!

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:19.000
Wow, you've finally come back
to "Child's Toy," huh?

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:23.460
You know, in life, there are peaks,
and there are valleys, and there are fields.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:25.130
Don't let it get you down,
cuz teapots are hot,

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.130
--and Osakan puhformuhs' front teeth
that stick out too far are their lives.
--Sana-chan, wait up.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.130
That's all for Zen-chan's appearance.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.390
That's awful! And here I came awl
the way from Osaka for this time...

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:33.720
You're being a pest!

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:37.350
Wait here a minute, okay? I'm going
to go call the producer, Gonda-san.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.730
From "Chaos Theater," right?

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:46.400
That's right! It was just a bit part,
yet they say he risked his life over it!

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.070
The strain was too much for him,
and he went belly-up!

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:51.070
He was such a joke of an actor!

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.410
All for a show such as that!

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:54.700
Or maybe I should call him a moronic actor!

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.410
Nah, his skills weren't all that great,
he wasn't so young anymore,

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.410
and anyone who might be eligible
for his wife ran away from him!

00:07:58.410 --> 00:07:59.750
Oh, I heard, I heard!

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:03.710
Something about how he was making time
with an elementary school girl.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:05.080
Let's see, his name was...

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.750
Gojo.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:12.430
Ah! Gonda-san! Be strong!

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:14.090
W- what are you doing, you brat!?

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.760
W- who do you think this gentleman is!?

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:19.100
Gojo Takeshi! That is his name!

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.770
What about it!?

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.100
This gentleman is a producer-

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:24.100
--I don't care!
--What!?

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.100
Who are you, then?

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.440
--And what's so wrong
about us talking bad about him?
--Huh? Where is Gonda-san?

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.770
Sana-chan!

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.440
Ah, you're Kurata-

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:33.400
Hello there! I am
Sana-chan's manager, Sagami!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.410
Allow me to do the
"Shaky I'm Sorry Dance" to apologize!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:37.070
Shaky-shaky-shaky-shaky...

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.410
Sana-chan!

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:44.040
I hate this, Take-chan!
Having them say those things!

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.920
Having them talk about you
like that, Take-chan,

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.420
after you worked as hard as you could!

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.920
I hate it!

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:56.090
Sana-chan didn't come
to school again today, huh?

00:08:57.090 --> 00:09:00.390
It's my fault! I don't know what I did,
but I'm sure it's my fault!

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:02.770
Why are you crying, Tsuyoshi-kun?
You're making Babbit-

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:05.060
Shut up.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.440
H- have you seen Sana-chan!?

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.730
Did something happen?

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:12.780
She ran out of the TV studio,
and now she's missing!

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:16.070
All right, let's use that
super-shaking vibrating machine!

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.110
It's a Burutcha!

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:19.160
That's not going to work.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.700
Sana-chan left her Burutcha home.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.000
Sana...

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.050
It was like this that other time, too.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:38.050
I wanted to be with Take-chan,
so I got on this train.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:40.760
Take-chan...

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.060
Sana-chan!

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:47.600
Come back, Sana-chan!

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:52.070
Kurata...

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:54.400
--Huh? Sana-chan?

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:59.070
That's right! It wasn't my fault,
but what am I supposed to do!?

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:00.410
Where's Sana-chan?

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.080
I'm looking for her, but nothing yet.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.580
We'll help you look too.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.750
Snow...

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:09.000
She might have...

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:13.130
Kurata might have gone there...

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.100
We'll always, always be together.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:26.520
He said we'd always be together.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:35.030
Take-chan...

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:36.690
Take-chan?

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.360
Hey.

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:43.370
Take-chan! I missed you! I missed you!

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:45.740
Take-chan!

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:52.380
It's you, Take-chan!
Take-chan, you're here by my side!

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:57.050
We'll be together always now,
Take-chan! Always!

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:58.720
Always!

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.050
We'll always be together!

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.060
♪ Drink up! Drink up! Drink some coffee! ♪

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.060
♪ Drink it up right now! Drink it all down! ♪

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:12.060
♪ Hot stuff, baby! Burn you up, honey! ♪

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:15.730
♪ Hot coffee! Here, thanks for waiting! ♪

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:17.740
Here, Take-chan.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:21.030
Sorry about earlier,
going home all by myself.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.070
But I'm not going home ever again.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:26.410
How about if I live here
together with you? And then...

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:29.250
...and then, we can always stay together.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:33.420
I'll never go anywhere again.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:39.220
I'll always be here with you, Take-chan.
Always, always. We'll always be together.

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:47.470
"Anas Ataruk!" What was that?

00:11:50.020 --> 00:11:52.650
It was "Kurata Sana!"

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:56.690
"Kobuchizawa Station"

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.690
Akito-kun, where is this?

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:56.690
Yatsugatake.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:59.360
How do you know that Sana-chan
would have come someplace like this?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.690
Some kind of wild instinct?

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:03.030
Oh, there's a juice can over here.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:07.660
It's true that Sana-chan came here before
when she was running after Gojo-san.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:09.040
The problem is...

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.710
...how are we going to get over there?

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.040
I wonder if the buses are running.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:16.710
It says here that they
are off during the winter.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.960
S- should we walk?

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:22.050
It's too cold.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.720
It's too far.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:25.590
Y- you're right.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:27.720
--How are we going to get

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:28.720
--all the way over there!?

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:31.520
--We give up! We give up!

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:34.350
--We throw up our hands and give up!

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:37.020
What's up with you guys? Need a lift?

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.360
--If you'd be so kind!

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.030
--Off, to Yatsugatake!

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:42.030
I ain't going there.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:44.030
--Huh? Why not?

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:45.360
Anywhere else would be okay,

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:47.530
but I'm not taking you
up to the mountains.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:51.370
That area is off limits
during this season, even to the locals.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:53.040
--Why? Why? Why?

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.790
Further, care must be
exercised near the peaks,

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.380
due to the risk of avalanche,
and in certain areas-

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:00.050
--A- avalanche!?

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.380
I- it can't be...

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:02.380
Sana-chan...

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:04.880
Come to think of it, I gave a ride
to a young girl this evening

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:07.390
who also said she wanted
to go to Yatsugatake.

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:10.060
W- was it a girl who looked like this?

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.060
Y- yeah...

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:13.060
She did come! Sana-chan is here!

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:15.060
--Where did Sana-chan go!?
--Where's Sana-chan!?

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:18.060
I took her to the base of the mountain,
but beyond that...

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:21.980
Please give us a lift as far
as you can, in any case.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.080
Bench!!

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:33.660
Young boys and girls,
twangy twangy twang!

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:37.000
Making out and giggling,
twangy twangy twang!

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.670
Take-chan, over here, over here!

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:40.000
Let's sit together.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:44.670
Like boyfriend and girlfriend.
Like father and daughter.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:49.640
In here, there won't be anyone to bother us,
and we can share each other's warmth!

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:56.690
I want us to stay like this always.
Always. Always.

00:13:56.690 --> 00:14:01.190
Always...

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.900
"Danger!! Frequent Avalanches
No Entry"

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:10.700
Oh, dear! The road has been blocked!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:14.040
Earlier, I dropped that girl off
just a little bit farther ahead.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.370
Up ahead, you say?

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:16.710
We can't go on any father.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:17.960
--Come on, come on, go, go!
--Can't you do something!?

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.540
--Fight! Attack!

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.040
--Don't lose, fight on!

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.960
--This is our chance!
--Hey, this looks like trouble.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:28.720
--Ava- Ava-

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.720
Avalanche!

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:38.730
--What is this, a spectacle anime!?

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:49.990
I wonder if Sana-chan is all right.
What do you think, Tsuyoshi-kun?

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:52.660
I don't know. What do
you think, Mami-chan?

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:55.040
I don't know. What do
you think, Hisae-chan?

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:58.000
Don't ask me. What do
you think, Aya-chan?

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:02.670
I don't know. What do
you think, Hayama-kun-

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:05.710
What do you think, Hayama-

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:07.710
Hayama-kun-

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:11.340
Hayama-kun isn't here!

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:18.350
Mister! Akito-kun... Akito-kun is gone!
He must have fallen out of the truck!

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:20.730
It wasn't my fault, though.

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:22.900
What do we do!? What do we do!?
Both Sana-chan and Akito-kun!

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:23.690
What do we do!?

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:26.730
I contacted the village authorities,

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.030
but in this snowstorm, it will be
impossible to search for them tonight.

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:30.740
--What!?

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:32.070
T- then...

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:33.070
What about Sana-chan?

00:15:33.070 --> 00:15:34.530
What about Akito-kun?

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:43.330
Babbit has arrived! Or whatever...

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:48.010
Babbit just wants to appear...
even if this is what I have to do...

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:50.090
Where am I?

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.010
That couldn't be...

00:15:57.010 --> 00:16:00.100
This thing fell down over there.

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:05.360
Hey, now, that's dangerous,
that's dangerous! You're scaring me!

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.020
This isn't on me, okay?

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:31.050
Place the center of your body
over your rear end, make a tight fist,

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:34.090
and strike! Strike! Strike!

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:38.640
Kurata!

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:41.770
If you're there, answer me!
Even if you're not there, answer me!

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.310
Ha... ya... ma?

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:48.320
What are you doing here?

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.320
What are you doing here, Hayama?

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:53.070
What? That's a good question...

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:55.110
Never mind, just come here!

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:57.320
There's no telling when
this thing is going to fall as it is!

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:58.990
No!

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:03.000
I'm staying here! I'm staying
here with him, forever and ever!

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.670
What are you talking about?

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:05.330
Grab on.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:08.380
No! I'm staying here with Take-chan!

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:13.050
I promised him that we'd be together.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:16.680
No matter what happened,
I'd stay together with Take-chan.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.350
We're staying together!

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:22.020
So, just leave me alone!

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:24.350
I can't.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:27.350
You're the one
who taught me before, remember?

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.230
That I should live...

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:33.320
that I should live as much as I can,
to make up for someone who died.

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.990
So I can't leave you alone.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:39.990
Hayama, your hand...
it's bleeding, isn't it?

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.330
It proves that I'm alive.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:44.000
Alive?

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:48.130
Earthworms, crickets, water striders...

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:52.000
I don't know if we're friends or not,
but as long as we're alive...

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:57.300
As long as we're alive?
As long as we're alive, what?

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:01.010
Take-chan?

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:03.140
Are you lonesome?

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:06.690
You died, leaving behind so many things
that you wanted to do.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:09.190
Are you lonesome, all by yourself?

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:14.530
Have I... become lonesome?

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:17.110
It's like suddenly,
I've been left all by myself...

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:25.700
Still... I'm sorry...

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:30.000
I'm sorry, Take-chan.
I have to... I have to...

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:38.630
Kurata...

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:41.640
Hold on to me tightly.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:44.970
If you let this life of mine go...

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:49.230
...you'll have to answer to me!

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:52.110
"Beware of avalanches"

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:52.150
Don't move, don't shout,
don't thrash about!

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:55.980
Let go! We're falling!

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:57.320
Shut up!

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:11.000
We made it! We're alive!

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.670
But, hey, where are we?

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.670
--Sana-chan!

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:17.010
Is that your name?

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:21.010
--Huh? What's going on? Huh? Huh?
--Thank goodness you're safe, Sana-chan!
Where have you been?

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:24.680
--To explain, they just fell
from here to here.
--We were worried!

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.680
Thank goodness, thank goodness.

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.600
Now, what's going on here!?

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:34.310
Uh, people of the village,
I'm terribly sorry for all the commotion.

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:37.610
I'm Kurata Sana, the one
who went missing last night.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:39.280
--Sana? She wouldn't be?
--As you can see,

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:42.320
--Oh, the one who is on TV?
--I'm safe now, so the search
will no longer be necessary.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.620
--Is that right?
--It's Sana-chan!

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.660
I've seen you on
"Late Night Chaos Theater"!

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:52.290
That man- Gojo-san, was it?-
he was a good actor.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:56.840
You two really seemed close,
like father and daughter.

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:05.010
Take-chan... all of these...

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:08.310
all of these people...

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:12.690
w- were watching you... Take-chan...

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:13.690
Sana-chan...

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:16.020
They saw Take-chan...

00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:20.110
They were watching Take-chan.
It wasn't just me.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:23.990
So many... so many other people...
saw Take-chan...

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:29.040
He was there! By my side!
By my side... my... my...

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:40.630
Take-chan, isn't this great? I'm not the
only one who remembers you, Take-chan...

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:47.640
...who knows that you
lived a full life, Take-chan...

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:51.220
Take-chan!!

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:57.310
I'm... home.

00:20:57.310 --> 00:21:00.650
You didn't catch cold?

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:02.320
I'm okay.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:04.990
I've been worried about you.

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:09.990
I'm sorry, Mama. I'm okay now.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:15.330
I'm okay... so... so...

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:17.380
I'm so sorry, Mama!

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:23.670
I'm so sorry... I'm so sorry...
I'm so sorry... I'm so sorry...

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:27.720
Welcome home, Sana.

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:33.020
I'm Kurata Sana, a 6th grader
and TV personality.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:35.520
Hayama Akito, my natural enemy,
my good friend,

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:37.020
and the one I owe my life to, I suppose.

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.360
The lovey-lovey Aya-chan and Tsuyoshi-kun,

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.690
not to mention Hisae-chan and Mami-chan.

00:21:41.690 --> 00:21:44.030
As well as everyone in the class!

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:48.030
We're all... we're all about
to graduate together.

00:21:48.030 --> 00:21:51.830
Okay, okay, let's finish
the monument now, okay?

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:55.370
--Each of us, tearfully,
--Graduation... when all of us
get a little sentimental...

00:21:55.370 --> 00:21:57.040
--Hey, get sentimental, would you!?
--Tearful, tearful, each of us, each of us!

00:21:57.040 --> 00:21:59.040
All right, done!

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.710
Sana-chan, you're good!

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:02.050
There you go! She's super-gifted!

00:22:02.050 --> 00:22:03.050
Oof.

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:05.720
Oomph.

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:08.050
Hey, you! Whaddya think you're doing!?

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:09.390
That way looks better. It's more real.

00:22:09.390 --> 00:22:11.390
What?

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:13.720
--Hmm, there might indeed
be some truth to that.
--Bye.

00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:16.390
Hey! Don't you mess with me!

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:19.060
--Even in middle school, those two...
--Fix it! Tearfully fix it!

00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:22.820
--...probably won't change.
--Hey, hold it! Get over here, you!

00:22:24.730 --> 00:22:29.740
With so many memories as souvenirs,
we'll all be going to middle school soon.

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:31.740
That's so campy.

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:33.330
Something wrong with that?

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:34.870
It's fine.

00:22:36.710 --> 00:22:39.000
It's all DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:41.840
When you sing this song, your worries will go

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:43.920
Bye Bye Bye

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:46.550
Cuz your heart will be carefree,

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:48.510
and your body will be healthy,

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:50.390
so resolve when to give up

00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:52.350
Bye Bye Bye Bye

00:22:52.350 --> 00:22:53.680
(Sing-ken-ken ken-ken)

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:55.520
(Tidak apa-apa,
Nday kambay kambay)

00:22:55.520 --> 00:22:57.980
It's always the same old nonsense,

00:22:58.100 --> 00:23:00.440
U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI U-MAI

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:03.020
(Mm? Could be you're fairly dumb...)

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:05.650
and then later comes the whimpering,

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:08.190
KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI KU-RAI

00:23:08.240 --> 00:23:10.990
(Ah... it's fine, it's fine, it's fine)

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:13.280
It's all crazy over there,

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:15.200
it's all "waah!" over here,

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:18.540
and the whole Earth
is spinning the wrong way.

00:23:18.660 --> 00:23:22.380
So at this point now, yeah at this point now,

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:26.670
you can laugh it away, excuse me, I must be going.

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:28.590
DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:31.430
When you sing this song, your worries will go

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:33.300
Bye Bye Bye

00:23:33.680 --> 00:23:36.140
Cuz you tried your MECHA-KUCHA best,

00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:38.060
to PECHA-KUCHA out a "Hi,"

00:23:38.180 --> 00:23:40.020
so just keep going unlike this!

00:23:40.140 --> 00:23:41.900
Wai Wai Wai Wai

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.810
DAIJO-BU DAIJO-BU

00:23:43.940 --> 00:23:48.740
Once your lips touch, you can't change your mind.

00:23:49.150 --> 00:23:51.400
Cuz your heart will be carefree,

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:53.320
and your body will be healthy,

00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:55.240
so resolve when to give up

00:23:55.410 --> 00:23:58.830
Bye Bye Bye Bye

00:23:58.910 --> 00:24:01.080
(Sing-ken-ken ken-ken,
Tidak apa-apa)

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:03.080
(Gwaenchansseumnida,
kwenchanayo)

00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:04.460
(Mou man tail)

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:11.970
Well then, what happens
to Sana-chan next time?

00:24:11.970 --> 00:24:14.640
Is hay fever the reason
why my nose is itching?

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:16.220
No it isn't, it looks like
it's because all the stories

00:24:16.220 --> 00:24:17.970
people are telling about me
are disturbing it.

00:24:17.970 --> 00:24:22.640
What's this? Oh, it appears that the topic
is my relationship with Hayama.

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:24.650
Next time on Kodomo no Omocha,
episode 51,

00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:28.650
the story of the investigative study into Sana-chan
and Hayama, plus what's going to happen next;

00:24:28.650 --> 00:24:32.320
"Up To Today, and As Of Tomorrow"

00:24:32.320 --> 00:24:35.780
Hay fever is something that
comes up on you without warning, achoo!
